# Runtime artifacts a run materializes locally — never part of the config.
# The config layer is TRACKED on purpose (issue #29): config.ts holds project
# decisions (labelBases, chainableBases, queue labels, base branch) that belong
# in review and in history — diffable, restorable, visible to every clone and
# to agents working in linked worktrees. Only what a machine generates below
# stays out: secrets (.env*), logs, agent worktrees, the out-of-tree Engine
# install (#22) with its local store and standalone lockfiles (#23). The examples are negated
# back in so `git archive` keeps shipping the templates.
.env*
!.env*.example
logs/
worktrees/
node_modules/
# Push-but-no-MR resume state (issue #26): a run materializes it when a branch
# was pushed but its MR never opened; the next round reads it back to resume.
publish-pending.json
.pnpm-store/
# One line per package manager adopt.ts can detect (its LOCKFILES table): the
# out-of-tree Engine install runs with cwd:.sandcastle/, so whichever manager the
# consumer uses writes ITS lockfile right here. Listing only npm's and pnpm's
# would let a yarn or bun consumer commit a generated lockfile the moment step 4
# stages the directory — the very leak #23 closed.
pnpm-lock.yaml
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
bun.lock
bun.lockb
